From: Tomasz Figa <tomasz.figa@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] net: dsa: qca8k: disable MAC-level LPI on all ports during setup

On QCA8337 switches, the hardware power-on reset default of the
QCA8K_REG_EEE_CTRL register (0x0100) is 0x00001550, which has MAC LPI
enabled on all internal ports (ports 1 through 5).

Because DSA and phylink do not invoke .set_mac_eee() at switch probe time
or port creation, the MAC-level LPI bits remain set to their reset defaults
until user space explicitly configures EEE via ethtool. On ports where EEE
is unsupported, disabled in Device Tree, or disabled at the PHY layer, this
results in the switch MAC attempting LPI signaling while the link partner
or PHY does not expect it.

Explicitly clear the LPI enable bits in QCA8K_REG_EEE_CTRL for all user
ports during qca8k_setup() so that ports start in a known, consistent
non-LPI state until explicitly enabled.

Fixes: 6b93fb664fb2 ("net-next: dsa: add new driver for QCA8K")
Signed-off-by: Tomasz Figa <tomasz.figa@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -2012,6 +2012,12 @@ qca8k_setup(struct dsa_switch *ds)
 				QCA8K_PORT_LOOKUP_MEMBER, 0);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
+
+		/* Disable EEE LPI by default on all ports */
+		ret = qca8k_rmw(priv, QCA8K_REG_EEE_CTRL,
+				QCA8K_REG_EEE_CTRL_LPI_EN(dp->index), 0);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
 	}
 
 	/* Disable MAC by default on all user ports */
